#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On a real quantum processor, noise turns the pure state $|\\psi\\rangle$ that a circuit is designed to prepare into a mixed state $\\rho$. Full quantum state tomography can reconstruct $\\rho$, but the number of measurements it needs grows exponentially with the number of qubits. Votto et al. [\\[1\\]](#references) instead learned a compact model of $\\rho$ for up to 96 qubits from randomized measurements. This tutorial follows their workflow.\n"
msgstr "Pada prosesor kuantum nyata, noise mengubah keadaan murni $|\\psi\\rangle$ yang dirancang untuk disiapkan oleh sebuah circuit menjadi keadaan campuran $\\rho$. Tomografi keadaan kuantum penuh bisa merekonstruksi $\\rho$, tapi jumlah pengukuran yang dibutuhkannya tumbuh secara eksponensial terhadap jumlah qubit. Votto dkk. [\\[1\\]](#references) sebaliknya mempelajari model ringkas dari $\\rho$ untuk hingga 96 qubit dari pengukuran acak. Tutorial ini mengikuti alur kerja mereka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a randomized measurement [\\[2\\]](#references), every qubit $i$ is rotated by an independent random unitary $u_i$ and then measured in the computational basis. One draw of the rotations is called a *measurement setting*, and each setting is repeated for $N_M$ shots. A shot with outcome bits $s_i$ gives the *classical shadow* [\\[3\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr "Pada pengukuran acak [\\[2\\]](#references), setiap qubit $i$ dirotasi oleh unitari acak independen $u_i$ lalu diukur dalam basis komputasi. Satu undian rotasi disebut *measurement setting*, dan setiap setting diulang sebanyak $N_M$ shot. Satu shot dengan bit hasil $s_i$ menghasilkan *classical shadow* [\\[3\\]](#references)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat\\rho=\\bigotimes_{i=1}^{N}\\left(3\\,u_i^\\dagger|s_i\\rangle\\langle s_i|u_i-\\mathbb{1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat\\rho=\\bigotimes_{i=1}^{N}\\left(3\\,u_i^\\dagger|s_i\\rangle\\langle s_i|u_i-\\mathbb{1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "whose average over settings and shots is $\\rho$. The prerequisite tutorial draws each $u_i$ from the three Pauli bases; this tutorial, like the paper, draws them uniformly from all single-qubit unitaries (Haar random), and the same formula applies.\n"
msgstr "yang rata-ratanya atas setting dan shot adalah $\\rho$. Tutorial prasyarat mengundi setiap $u_i$ dari tiga basis Pauli; tutorial ini, seperti makalahnya, mengundinya secara seragam dari semua unitari satu-qubit (Haar random), dan rumus yang sama berlaku.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shadows estimate properties of a few qubits at a time. The paper combines them into a *matrix product operator* (MPO), which writes the density matrix as a chain of small tensors, one per qubit; noisy states with short-range correlations need only small bonds between neighboring tensors. Like the density matrix renormalization group (DMRG) algorithm, the learner sweeps along the chain and updates one tensor at a time, so that the model matches the shadows on the window of $2\\ell+1$ qubits centered on that tensor (Equation 4 of the paper). The bond dimension stays fixed during these updates, so the learner never truncates the model. Because data enter only through these windows, the number of settings needed does not grow with the length of the chain.\n"
msgstr "Shadow memperkirakan properti beberapa qubit sekaligus. Makalah ini menggabungkannya menjadi *matrix product operator* (MPO), yang menuliskan matriks densitas sebagai rantai tensor kecil, satu per qubit; keadaan bernoise dengan korelasi jarak pendek hanya membutuhkan bond kecil di antara tensor yang bertetangga. Seperti algoritma density matrix renormalization group (DMRG), learner menyapu sepanjang rantai dan memperbarui satu tensor sekaligus, sehingga model cocok dengan shadow pada jendela $2\\ell+1$ qubit yang berpusat pada tensor itu (Persamaan 4 dalam makalah). Dimensi bond tetap selama pembaruan ini, jadi learner tidak pernah memotong model. Karena data hanya masuk lewat jendela-jendela ini, jumlah setting yang dibutuhkan tidak bertambah seiring panjang rantai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The settings are split into a training set and a testing set. On the testing set, the paper estimates the max fidelity between $\\rho$ and the model $\\sigma$,\n"
msgstr "Setting dibagi menjadi set pelatihan dan set pengujian. Pada set pengujian, makalah memperkirakan fidelitas maksimum antara $\\rho$ dan model $\\sigma$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}(\\rho,\\sigma)=\\frac{\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)}{\\max\\left(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2,\\ \\mathrm{tr}\\,\\sigma^2\\right)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}(\\rho,\\sigma)=\\frac{\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)}{\\max\\left(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2,\\ \\mathrm{tr}\\,\\sigma^2\\right)}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ directly would take exponentially many measurements. Instead, the paper assumes the *approximate factorization condition* (AFC): correlations in $\\rho$ decay within a few qubits, so global overlaps and purities factor into terms on blocks of $k$ neighboring qubits. The purity also gives the Rényi-2 entropy $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2$, which measures how mixed the state is.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ secara langsung akan membutuhkan pengukuran dalam jumlah eksponensial. Sebagai gantinya, makalah mengasumsikan *approximate factorization condition* (AFC): korelasi di $\\rho$ meluruh dalam beberapa qubit, sehingga overlap dan purity global terfaktorkan menjadi suku-suku pada blok $k$ qubit bertetangga. Purity juga memberikan entropi Rényi-2 $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2$, yang mengukur seberapa campuran keadaan tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The paper prepares the depth-$D$ kicked-Ising state\n"
msgstr "Makalah menyiapkan keadaan kicked-Ising berkedalaman $D$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle=\\left(\\prod_{j} e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}\\prod_j e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X_j}\\right)^{D}|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle=\\left(\\prod_{j} e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}\\prod_j e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X_j}\\right)^{D}|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "on 96 qubits of `ibm_brisbane`, an Eagle processor, with 2,048 settings of 1,024 shots for $D=1$. Figure 1(c,d) of the paper reports two results for $D=1$:\n"
msgstr "pada 96 qubit `ibm_brisbane`, prosesor Eagle, dengan 2.048 setting masing-masing 1.024 shot untuk $D=1$. Gambar 1(c,d) dalam makalah melaporkan dua hasil untuk $D=1$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learned model reaches $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}\\approx 75\\%$ with the experimental state at $N=96$, far above the overlap of the ideal state $|\\psi\\rangle$ with the experiment.\n"
msgstr "Model yang dipelajari mencapai $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}\\approx 75\\%$ dengan keadaan eksperimen pada $N=96$, jauh di atas overlap keadaan ideal $|\\psi\\rangle$ dengan eksperimen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entropy grows linearly, $S_2\\approx(0.14\\text{ to }0.15)\\,N$, and the entropy of the model agrees with an independent estimate from the testing set.\n"
msgstr "Entropi tumbuh secara linear, $S_2\\approx(0.14\\text{ sampai }0.15)\\,N$, dan entropi model sesuai dengan perkiraan independen dari set pengujian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial checks both results, first in an eight-qubit simulation where the exact answers are known, and then in a new 96-qubit run on `ibm_fez`, a Heron r2 processor. The learner is an independent Julia implementation of the equations in the paper and its supplement.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini memeriksa kedua hasil tersebut, pertama dalam simulasi delapan qubit di mana jawaban eksaknya diketahui, lalu dalam run 96-qubit baru pada `ibm_fez`, prosesor Heron r2. Learner-nya adalah implementasi Julia independen dari persamaan-persamaan dalam makalah dan suplemennya.\n"

