# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Setup {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The helper module [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), which the Setup cell downloads, implements the learner. The tutorial calls the following functions from it:\n"
msgstr "Modul helper [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), yang diunduh oleh cell Setup, mengimplementasikan learner. Tutorial memanggil fungsi-fungsi berikut darinya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Function | Purpose |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | Exact MPO of the ideal kicked-Ising state, or of the state after local depolarizing noise |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Randomly assign measurement settings to training and testing sets (half each by default) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Shadow estimates of every learning window, from the training settings only |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior for common randomized measurements (CRM), fitted to the measured purity of each window, as in the paper |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Sweep the one-site update of the paper along the chain, starting from the maximally mixed state |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | Exact $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ between two MPOs |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | AFC estimates of $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ from the testing settings, with jackknife error bars |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Fungsi | Tujuan |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | MPO eksak dari keadaan kicked-Ising ideal, atau dari keadaan setelah noise depolarisasi lokal |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Menetapkan measurement setting secara acak ke set pelatihan dan pengujian (masing-masing separuh secara default) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Estimasi shadow dari setiap jendela pembelajaran, hanya dari setting pelatihan |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior untuk common randomized measurements (CRM), di-fit ke purity terukur dari setiap jendela, seperti dalam makalah |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Menyapu pembaruan satu-site dari makalah sepanjang rantai, mulai dari keadaan campuran maksimal |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ eksak dan $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ antara dua MPO |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | Estimasi AFC dari $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ dan $S_2$ dari setting pengujian, dengan error bar jackknife |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learner stores the MPO in the Pauli basis. This keeps the model Hermitian with unit trace, but it does not force the model to be positive semidefinite, so the notebook reports how negative its eigenvalues become.\n"
msgstr "Learner menyimpan MPO dalam basis Pauli. Ini menjaga model tetap Hermitian dengan trace satu, tapi tidak memaksa model menjadi semidefinit positif, jadi notebook melaporkan seberapa negatif nilai eigennya.\n"

