# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The residual measures how far the model's windows are from the training shadows. It drops when the one-site updates start, in the second sweep, and then stays approximately constant instead of reaching zero, because the shadows contain statistical noise that a model with a small bond dimension cannot reproduce.\n"
msgstr "Residual mengukur seberapa jauh jendela model dari shadow pelatihan. Nilainya turun saat pembaruan satu-site dimulai, di sweep kedua, lalu tetap kira-kira konstan alih-alih mencapai nol, karena shadow mengandung noise statistik yang tidak bisa direproduksi oleh model dengan dimensi bond kecil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because this state is known, you can compare the learned model with it exactly, and also compare the two simplest guesses with it: the CRM prior and the ideal state.\n"
msgstr "Karena keadaan ini diketahui, kamu bisa membandingkan model yang dipelajari dengannya secara eksak, dan juga membandingkan dua tebakan paling sederhana dengannya: prior CRM dan keadaan ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learned model is closer to the noisy state than either the prior or the ideal state, so it has learned the noise from the data. Its small negative eigenvalues come from the finite number of measurements.\n"
msgstr "Model yang dipelajari lebih dekat ke keadaan bernoise daripada prior maupun keadaan ideal, jadi ia sudah mempelajari noise dari data. Nilai eigen negatifnya yang kecil berasal dari jumlah pengukuran yang terbatas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, the state is unknown, so you estimate $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ from the testing settings instead. AFC splits the chain into blocks $A_1,\\dots,A_R$ of $k$ qubits and approximates the purity by\n"
msgstr "Pada perangkat keras, keadaannya tidak diketahui, jadi kamu memperkirakan $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ dari setting pengujian. AFC membagi rantai menjadi blok $A_1,\\dots,A_R$ yang masing-masing berisi $k$ qubit dan mengaproksimasi purity dengan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2\\approx\\frac{\\prod_{i=1}^{R-1}\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_{A_iA_{i+1}}^2}{\\prod_{i=2}^{R-1}\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_{A_i}^2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2\\approx\\frac{\\prod_{i=1}^{R-1}\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_{A_iA_{i+1}}^2}{\\prod_{i=2}^{R-1}\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_{A_i}^2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ by the same ratio of local overlaps. With $k=4$, the two blocks cover all eight qubits and the formula is exact; with $k=2$, it relies on the factorization assumption. The jackknife error bars, which leave out one testing setting at a time, cover the statistical error of the testing data only, not the randomness of training or the AFC approximation.\n"
msgstr "dan $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ dengan rasio overlap lokal yang sama. Dengan $k=4$, kedua blok mencakup semua delapan qubit dan rumusnya eksak; dengan $k=2$, ia bergantung pada asumsi faktorisasi. Error bar jackknife, yang menyisihkan satu setting pengujian setiap kali, hanya mencakup kesalahan statistik data pengujian, bukan keacakan pelatihan atau aproksimasi AFC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
