msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-1}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi di hardware kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A chain is only as good as its worst qubit, so choose the 96 physical qubits yourself. The `transpile` function of `Qiskit.jl` cannot yet accept a fixed initial layout, and in a test on `ibm_phoenix`, the layout it chose included a qubit with 51% readout error. The following chain is the 96-qubit path in the `ibm_fez` coupling map that the error-aware layout of the Python Qiskit `transpile` function (with `optimization_level=3`) selected from the calibration data of 27 September 2026. Its mean readout error is 1.6%, but a heavy-hex lattice has few 96-qubit paths, and this one includes qubit 35, which has a 15% readout error. Calibrations change, so choose a new chain from the current [calibration data](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) before you run on another day or QPU.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah rantai hanya sebaik qubit terburuknya, jadi pilih sendiri 96 qubit fisiknya. Fungsi `transpile` dari `Qiskit.jl` belum bisa menerima initial layout yang tetap, dan dalam uji di `ibm_phoenix`, layout yang dipilihnya menyertakan satu qubit dengan error pembacaan 51%. Rantai berikut adalah jalur 96 qubit di coupling map `ibm_fez` yang dipilih oleh layout sadar-error dari fungsi `transpile` Qiskit Python (dengan `optimization_level=3`) berdasarkan data kalibrasi tanggal 27 September 2026. Rata-rata error pembacaannya 1,6%, tetapi kisi heavy-hex punya sedikit jalur 96 qubit, dan jalur ini menyertakan qubit 35 yang error pembacaannya 15%. Kalibrasi berubah-ubah, jadi pilih rantai baru dari [data kalibrasi](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) terkini sebelum kamu menjalankan di hari lain atau di QPU lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep this chain, write the circuits directly in native gates instead of transpiling them. A $U(\\theta,\\phi,\\lambda)$ gate equals $R_Z(\\phi+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\theta+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\lambda)$ up to a global phase. This decomposition covers both the random rotations and the kick $e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X}=U(\\pi/4,-\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$. The gate $e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}$ equals a CZ gate followed by $S^\\dagger$ on both qubits, up to a global phase. Because these $S^\\dagger$ gates are diagonal, they commute with the CZ gates, so each qubit collects one $R_Z(-\\pi/2)$ per bond before its measurement rotation.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mempertahankan rantai ini, tulis circuit langsung dalam native gate, bukan men-transpile-nya. Sebuah gate $U(\\theta,\\phi,\\lambda)$ sama dengan $R_Z(\\phi+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\theta+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\lambda)$ sampai fase global. Dekomposisi ini mencakup rotasi acak sekaligus kick $e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X}=U(\\pi/4,-\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$. Gate $e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}$ sama dengan gate CZ yang diikuti $S^\\dagger$ pada kedua qubit, sampai fase global. Karena gate $S^\\dagger$ ini diagonal, keduanya komut dengan gate CZ, jadi setiap qubit mengumpulkan satu $R_Z(-\\pi/2)$ per ikatan sebelum rotasi pengukurannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-1}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` runs one circuit per Sampler job, so collecting the data requires 1,024 jobs. The following cell keeps up to 32 jobs in the queue and saves the outcomes of each setting as soon as its job finishes. Each shot is returned as a vector of bits, in which element $i$ is the outcome of chain qubit $i$.\n"
msgstr "`QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` menjalankan satu circuit per job Sampler, jadi pengumpulan data membutuhkan 1.024 job. Cell berikut menjaga hingga 32 job di antrean dan menyimpan hasil tiap setelan begitu job-nya selesai. Setiap shot dikembalikan sebagai vektor bit, dengan elemen $i$ adalah hasil dari qubit rantai ke-$i$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You must retrieve the results in the same session that submitted the jobs, because `QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` cannot yet look up a job by its ID ([qiskit-ibm-runtime-c issue #28](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime-c/issues/28)). If a job fails, the cell issues a warning and continues. If the session stops, run Steps 1 through 3 again. Rerunning the cell submits only the settings whose outcomes are missing. With `use_saved_data = true`, the cell submits nothing.\n"
msgstr "Kamu harus mengambil hasilnya di Session yang sama dengan yang mengirim job, karena `QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` belum bisa mencari job berdasarkan ID-nya ([qiskit-ibm-runtime-c issue #28](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime-c/issues/28)). Kalau sebuah job gagal, cell ini mengeluarkan peringatan dan lanjut. Kalau Session berhenti, jalankan lagi Langkah 1 sampai 3. Menjalankan ulang cell hanya mengirim setelan yang hasilnya belum ada. Dengan `use_saved_data = true`, cell tidak mengirim apa pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format-1}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This step reads only saved data: the downloaded `ibm_fez` run if `use_saved_data` is true, or otherwise the files that Step 3 wrote. You can therefore run it in a new session without submitting jobs (run the Setup cell, the `use_saved_data` cell, and Step 1 first). The downloaded file stores the 96 outcomes of each shot packed into 12 bytes, most significant bit first, so the loader unpacks them. `RandomMeas.jl` labels outcomes 1 and 2, so the loader also adds 1 to every bit.\n"
msgstr "Langkah ini hanya membaca data tersimpan: hasil run `ibm_fez` yang diunduh kalau `use_saved_data` bernilai true, atau kalau tidak, file yang ditulis Langkah 3. Jadi kamu bisa menjalankannya di Session baru tanpa mengirim job (jalankan dulu cell Setup, cell `use_saved_data`, dan Langkah 1). File yang diunduh menyimpan 96 hasil tiap shot yang dikemas dalam 12 byte, bit paling signifikan lebih dulu, jadi loader membongkarnya. `RandomMeas.jl` memberi label hasil 1 dan 2, jadi loader juga menambahkan 1 ke setiap bit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before learning, check the data. A broken qubit or a badly calibrated gate makes the measured state much more mixed around it, and it can make the learner diverge. The purity of a few neighboring qubits is a model-free benchmark of this noise: the function `get_purity` from `RandomMeas.jl` estimates $\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_A^2$ for a subsystem $A$ by comparing pairs of shots from the same setting. Compute the Rényi-2 entropy $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_A^2$ of every window of six neighboring qubits, and compare it with the same window of the ideal state. The ideal value is not zero, because each window is entangled with the rest of the chain; noise increases it, and a broken qubit pushes every window that contains it toward the maximum of six.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum belajar, periksa datanya. Qubit yang rusak atau gate yang kalibrasinya buruk membuat state yang diukur jauh lebih campur di sekitarnya, dan bisa membuat learner divergen. Purity dari beberapa qubit bertetangga adalah tolok ukur bebas-model untuk noise ini: fungsi `get_purity` dari `RandomMeas.jl` memperkirakan $\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_A^2$ untuk subsistem $A$ dengan membandingkan pasangan shot dari setelan yang sama. Hitung entropi Rényi-2 $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_A^2$ untuk setiap jendela enam qubit bertetangga, lalu bandingkan dengan jendela yang sama pada state ideal. Nilai idealnya bukan nol, karena setiap jendela terentang (entangled) dengan sisa rantai; noise menaikkannya, dan qubit yang rusak mendorong setiap jendela yang memuatnya ke arah maksimum enam.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
