# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The results reproduce both claims of the paper on a different processor:\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya mereproduksi kedua klaim makalah di prosesor yang berbeda:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The model describes the data far better than the ideal state.** At $N=96$, the held-out $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ of the $\\ell=2$ model is 0.59 ± 0.10, compared with 0.0035 for the ideal state. The paper reports about 0.75 on `ibm_brisbane`.\n"
msgstr "**Model menjelaskan data jauh lebih baik daripada state ideal.** Pada $N=96$, $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ held-out dari model $\\ell=2$ adalah 0,59 ± 0,10, dibandingkan 0,0035 untuk state ideal. Makalah melaporkan sekitar 0,75 di `ibm_brisbane`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The entropy of the model agrees with the testing data at every $N$.** At $N=96$, it is 10.2 from the model and 10.0 ± 0.3 from the testing data, or $S_2/N\\approx 0.10$, compared with 0.14 to 0.15 on the older `ibm_brisbane`.\n"
msgstr "**Entropi model cocok dengan data pengujian di setiap $N$.** Pada $N=96$, nilainya 10,2 dari model dan 10,0 ± 0,3 dari data pengujian, atau $S_2/N\\approx 0.10$, dibandingkan 0,14 sampai 0,15 di `ibm_brisbane` yang lebih lama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The comparison of window sizes shows where the information is. With $\\ell=1$, the model is almost as good ($\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}=0.55\\pm0.09$), so for these data, correlations beyond a few qubits add little. With $\\ell=0$, the product state misses the entanglement between neighboring qubits: its entropy grows to 32 instead of 10, and its $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ falls even faster than that of the ideal state, to $6\\times10^{-6}$ at $N=96$.\n"
msgstr "Perbandingan ukuran jendela menunjukkan di mana informasinya berada. Dengan $\\ell=1$, modelnya hampir sama bagusnya ($\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}=0.55\\pm0.09$), jadi untuk data ini, korelasi di luar beberapa qubit hanya menambah sedikit. Dengan $\\ell=0$, product state melewatkan entanglement antar qubit bertetangga: entropinya naik jadi 32 alih-alih 10, dan $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$-nya turun bahkan lebih cepat daripada state ideal, jadi $6\\times10^{-6}$ pada $N=96$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following limitations in mind when you read these numbers:\n"
msgstr "Ingat batasan-batasan berikut saat membaca angka-angka ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Training split.** The error bars cover the statistical error of the testing data only. Other random splits of the same settings give $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ between 0.49 and 0.59 at $N=96$ for $\\ell=2$.\n"
msgstr "**Pembagian pelatihan.** Error bar hanya mencakup error statistik dari data pengujian. Pembagian acak lain dari setelan yang sama memberi $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ antara 0,49 dan 0,59 pada $N=96$ untuk $\\ell=2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Final sweep.** The learner always returns the model from the final sweep, so the testing data never influence the model.\n"
msgstr "**Sweep terakhir.** Learner selalu mengembalikan model dari sweep terakhir, jadi data pengujian tidak pernah memengaruhi model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Positivity.** The model is not constrained to be positive semidefinite; its most negative eigenvalue in a learning window is about $-0.05$. Its $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ therefore describe an operator, not certified properties of a physical state.\n"
msgstr "**Positivitas.** Model tidak dibatasi untuk positif semidefinit; eigenvalue paling negatifnya dalam sebuah jendela pembelajaran sekitar $-0.05$. Jadi $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ dan $S_2$-nya menggambarkan sebuah operator, bukan properti tersertifikasi dari state fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Factorization.** Every held-out estimate relies on the AFC assumption, which the measurements themselves cannot certify.\n"
msgstr "**Faktorisasi.** Setiap estimasi held-out bergantung pada asumsi AFC, yang tidak bisa disertifikasi oleh pengukuran itu sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah selanjutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Rekomendasi\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the experiment at depth two with the paper's parameters for that depth ($\\ell=3$ and a maximum bond dimension of 8), and determine how many measurement settings the learner needs.\n"
msgstr "Ulangi eksperimen pada kedalaman dua dengan parameter makalah untuk kedalaman itu ($\\ell=3$ dan dimensi ikatan maksimum 8), lalu tentukan berapa banyak setelan pengukuran yang dibutuhkan learner.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn with the two-site update instead (`update=:two_site` in `training_marginals` and `learn_mpo`), which truncates the bond dimension after every step, and see how it behaves with fewer training settings.\n"
msgstr "Belajar dengan pembaruan dua-situs (`update=:two_site` di `training_marginals` dan `learn_mpo`), yang memangkas dimensi ikatan setelah setiap langkah, dan lihat bagaimana perilakunya dengan lebih sedikit setelan pelatihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn without the CRM prior (`prior=nothing`) and compare the held-out fidelity.\n"
msgstr "Belajar tanpa prior CRM (`prior=nothing`) dan bandingkan fidelity held-out-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the same analysis to the authors' published [`ibm_brisbane` measurements](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18323569).\n"
msgstr "Terapkan analisis yang sama pada [pengukuran `ibm_brisbane`](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18323569) yang dipublikasikan para penulis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the [supplement of the paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.12550) for the derivation of the update and of the AFC estimators.\n"
msgstr "Baca [suplemen makalah](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.12550) untuk penurunan rumus pembaruan dan estimator AFC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explore other randomized-measurement protocols in the [`RandomMeas.jl` examples](https://github.com/bvermersch/RandomMeas.jl/tree/main/examples).\n"
msgstr "Jelajahi protokol pengukuran acak lainnya di [contoh `RandomMeas.jl`](https://github.com/bvermersch/RandomMeas.jl/tree/main/examples).\n"

